["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Deer bed on benches, cross at saddles and feed on edges. A topo map shows all three from your kitchen table.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How contour lines are made. Top: side view of a hill, steep on the left, gentle on the right, cut by three flat slices. Bottom: the map view, where each slice becomes a ring. Rings sit close together on the steep side and far apart on the gentle side.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Side view</text>\n  <path d=\"M40 140 L80 120 L120 70 L145 40 L170 50 L240 90 L340 140 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"115\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"65\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"84\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"225\"/><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"225\"/><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"225\"/>\n    <line x1=\"196\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"225\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"225\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"225\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Map view</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"187\" cy=\"225\" rx=\"103\" ry=\"48\"/><ellipse cx=\"172\" cy=\"225\" rx=\"68\" ry=\"33\"/><ellipse cx=\"160\" cy=\"225\" rx=\"36\" ry=\"18\"/>\n  </g>\n  <circle cx=\"148\" cy=\"225\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"392\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Each slice</text>\n  <text x=\"392\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">= one line</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Steep: lines close</text>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">Gentle: far apart</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Each contour line is one flat slice of the hill <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Close lines: steep. Far apart: gentle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: topo map basics</summary><ul><li>A topo (topographic) map shows the shape of the ground with contour lines <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Canada's standard sheets are the NTS (National Topographic System) at 1:50,000 and 1:250,000 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Every phone map app draws the same contours. Learn them once, use them everywhere.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map scale ruler. On a 1 to 50,000 map, 1 centimetre is 500 metres on the ground, so 2 centimetres, about a thumb width, is 1 kilometre, about 20 to 30 minutes of walking in hills. On a 1 to 250,000 map, 1 centimetre is 2.5 kilometres.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1:50,000 map</text>\n  <g>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"50\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"50\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"50\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"50\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"40\" y=\"92\">0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\">1 cm</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"92\">2 cm</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"92\">3 cm</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"92\">4 cm</text>\n    <text x=\"40\" y=\"110\">0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\">500 m</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"110\">1 km</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"110\">1.5 km</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"110\">2 km</text>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M40 130 L200 130\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"40,122 40,138 30,130\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><polygon points=\"200,122 200,138 210,130\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"145\" width=\"80\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#c9b79c\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thumb</text>\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Thumb about 2 cm</text>\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">= 1 km on the ground</text>\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">= 20 to 30 min in hills</text>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"218\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1:250,000 map</text>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"258\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <text x=\"130\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">1 cm = 2.5 km. Driving only</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>1 cm on the map is 500 m on the ground <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>A thumb, about 2 cm, is 1 km: 20 to 30 minutes of walking (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: scale details</summary><ul><li>1:50,000 means 1 unit on the map is 50,000 units on the ground. 1 cm on the map is 500 m on the ground <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>1:250,000: 1 cm is 2.5 km <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Good for driving, useless for picking a bench.</li><li>One 1:50,000 sheet covers about 1,000 square km <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Rule of thumb at 1:50,000: a thumb width, about 2 cm, is 1 km (Tip).</li><li>Walking speed in hills is about 2 to 3 km per hour, so a thumb is 20 to 30 minutes (Tip).</li><li>North is at the top of an NTS (National Topographic System) map <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Contour lines on a slope. On the left the lines bunch close together: steep. On the right they spread far apart: gentle. One thicker index line carries the height number 1200, and the top of the number faces uphill.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"230\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <path d=\"M10 120 C 140 116, 260 70, 390 60\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 132 C 140 130, 260 104, 390 100\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 156 C 140 156, 260 172, 390 180\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 168 C 140 170, 260 206, 390 220\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 180 C 140 184, 260 240, 390 260\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M10 144 C 140 143, 260 138, 390 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"226\" y=\"124\" width=\"52\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"252\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1200</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Uphill this way</text>\n  <path d=\"M352 50 L352 20\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"344,24 360,24 352,10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Steep</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">lines close</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Gentle</text>\n  <text x=\"290\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">far apart</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thick line = index, has the height number</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The thick line carries the height. The top of the number faces uphill <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>The height step between lines is printed in the map margin <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: contour line details</summary><ul><li>A contour line joins points of equal elevation <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Lines close together: steep. Lines far apart: gentle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>The contour interval is the height step between lines. It is printed in the map margin and varies by sheet <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Newer sheets use 20 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Check the margin.</li><li>Every fifth line is thicker, the index contour, and carries a number <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>The numbers read uphill: the top of the number points up the slope <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Colours on NTS (National Topographic System) sheets: brown contours, blue water, green wooded, white open ground <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Water runs in draws. Arrows and falls symbols show which way it flows <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"5\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Five shapes to find on any topo</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 5</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map view of a ridge. Nested U shaped contour lines point downhill, toward the bottom of the page. An orange dashed line runs down the spine of the ridge.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <path d=\"M150 36 C 150 110, 250 110, 250 36\"/>\n    <path d=\"M120 36 C 120 150, 280 150, 280 36\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 36 C 90 190, 310 190, 310 36\"/>\n    <path d=\"M60 36 C 60 230, 340 230, 340 36\"/>\n    <path d=\"M30 36 C 30 268, 370 268, 370 36\"/>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"262\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"10 6\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Ridge</text>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">High ground at top</text>\n  <text x=\"208\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">spine</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">U or V points DOWNHILL</text>\n  <polygon points=\"360,240 376,240 368,256\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"368\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Ridge: the Vs point downhill.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map view of a draw, a small valley. Nested V shaped contour lines point uphill, toward the top of the page. A blue creek runs down through the points of the Vs.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <path d=\"M30 70 L200 50 L370 70\"/>\n    <path d=\"M30 120 L200 90 L370 120\"/>\n    <path d=\"M30 170 L200 130 L370 170\"/>\n    <path d=\"M30 220 L200 172 L370 220\"/>\n    <path d=\"M30 262 L200 214 L370 262\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M200 44 C 196 100, 206 150, 198 200 S 202 250, 200 268\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Draw</text>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">High ground at top</text>\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">water runs down</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V points UPHILL</text>\n  <polygon points=\"360,58 376,58 368,42\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"368\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"88\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Draw: the Vs point uphill. Water runs here.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map view of a saddle. Two peaks, each a set of closed loops, sit left and right. The lines between them pinch into an hourglass. The low point in the middle is the saddle, and a deer trail crosses the ridge there.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"22\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"45\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"22\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"45\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 125 C 170 85, 30 70, 30 150 C 30 230, 170 215, 200 175 C 230 215, 370 230, 370 150 C 370 70, 230 85, 200 125 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 92 C 150 50, 10 40, 10 150 C 10 260, 150 250, 200 208 C 250 250, 390 260, 390 150 C 390 40, 250 50, 200 92 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M200 40 C 210 90, 190 120, 200 150 S 190 220, 205 268\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dotted = deer trail</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hourglass = low crossing point</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Saddle: the hourglass between two peaks. Deer cross here.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map view of a bench. Tight contour lines above and below a wide gap. The wide gap, shaded orange, is a flat step on the slope where a deer lies bedded. A small side view shows the step shape.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 82 C 120 76, 260 90, 400 84 L400 168 C 260 176, 120 160, 0 166 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <path d=\"M0 50 C 120 44, 260 58, 400 52\"/><path d=\"M0 66 C 120 60, 260 74, 400 68\"/><path d=\"M0 82 C 120 76, 260 90, 400 84\"/>\n    <path d=\"M0 166 C 120 160, 260 176, 400 168\"/><path d=\"M0 182 C 120 176, 260 192, 400 184\"/><path d=\"M0 198 C 120 192, 260 208, 400 200\"/><path d=\"M0 214 C 120 208, 260 224, 400 216\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(110 128)\">\n    <ellipse rx=\"20\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M15 -15 l-4 -9 M21 -15 l4 -9\" stroke=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench: wide gap</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Bench</text>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">High ground at top</text>\n  <rect x=\"250\" y=\"226\" width=\"140\" height=\"66\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M258 236 L300 262 L345 264 L382 288\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">side view</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tight lines above and below</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Bench: a wide gap between tight lines. Deer bed here.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map view of a cliff. Several contour lines squeeze together until they touch in the middle. A red X marks the cliff. An orange dashed route goes around the end of it instead.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <path d=\"M10 70 C 120 74, 160 142, 200 148 C 240 142, 280 74, 390 70\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 100 C 120 104, 160 146, 200 150 C 240 146, 280 104, 390 100\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 200 C 120 196, 160 154, 200 152 C 240 154, 280 196, 390 200\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 230 C 120 226, 160 156, 200 154 C 240 156, 280 226, 390 230\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M186 136 L214 164 M214 136 L186 164\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 260 C 40 180, 40 120, 60 50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"52,56 68,56 60,40\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">go around</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Cliff</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lines touch = cliff. No route here</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>5.</b> Cliff: lines touch. Plan around it.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every shape, in words</summary><ul><li><strong>Ridge:</strong> a long high spine. Contours make U or V shapes that point downhill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Draw:</strong> a small valley running down a slope. Contours make V shapes that point uphill, toward the high ground <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Draws carry water, cool air and deer.</li><li><strong>Saddle:</strong> the low point on a ridge between two highs. Two sets of closed loops with an hourglass between them <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Deer cross ridges at saddles <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Hunter observation.</li><li><strong>Bench:</strong> a flat step on a slope. A wide gap between lines with tight lines above and below <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Deer bed on benches with a view <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Hunter observation.</li><li><strong>Spur:</strong> a short ridge running off the main ridge. Contours point downhill, like a tongue <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Cliff:</strong> lines touch or merge. Do not plan a route through them <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Knob or peak:</strong> small closed loops. A glassing seat if it looks across a bench (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 540\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"ct-arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"540\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Side view of the hill</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"80\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"110\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"140\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"170\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"200\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"85\">1400 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"115\">1300 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"145\">1200 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"175\">1100 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"205\">1000 m</text>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M 60,218 C 75,212 90,195 105,170 C 120,140 140,100 160,82 C 170,73 182,72 190,80 C 200,92 212,112 222,124 C 230,132 240,132 248,124 C 258,112 268,96 278,86 C 284,80 292,80 298,88 C 310,110 316,150 322,166 L 350,168 C 362,170 376,196 390,218 L 395,218 L 395,232 L 60,232 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"178\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"236\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"354\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Steep</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">lines close</text>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same hill from above: contours</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <path d=\"M 15,395 C 15,330 80,300 140,300 C 185,300 196,335 220,348 C 246,360 256,328 290,325 C 360,322 398,372 394,420 C 388,458 350,478 300,476 C 270,476 255,480 245,478 C 232,476 226,440 218,432 C 210,440 200,478 182,480 C 152,484 120,482 100,474 C 60,464 32,450 14,425 C 6,412 8,402 15,395 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 35,395 C 35,345 90,318 140,318 C 180,318 192,348 216,360 C 240,372 250,345 286,342 C 340,340 390,372 386,418 C 380,448 350,462 302,460 C 282,459 264,462 252,460 C 240,458 230,432 218,422 C 206,432 196,458 182,460 C 155,463 128,462 108,456 C 76,448 50,440 36,418 C 29,408 30,400 35,395 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 62,392 C 62,350 108,332 140,334 C 172,336 186,360 212,372 C 234,382 246,362 282,360 C 326,358 350,382 346,412 C 342,438 322,448 290,446 C 262,444 246,428 214,422 C 196,422 182,446 142,448 C 100,450 62,430 62,392 Z\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"388\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"26\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"400\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"22\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"388\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"12\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"400\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"11\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 112,357 Q 140,347 168,357\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 110,352 Q 140,341 170,352\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 108,347 Q 140,335 172,347\"/>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"388\" x2=\"288\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"393\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"405\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"407\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ridge</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ct-arrow)\">\n    <line x1=\"214\" y1=\"302\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"382\"/>\n    <line x1=\"84\" y1=\"302\" x2=\"118\" y2=\"342\"/>\n    <line x1=\"236\" y1=\"498\" x2=\"221\" y2=\"440\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"512\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"432\"/>\n    <line x1=\"366\" y1=\"482\" x2=\"366\" y2=\"420\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cliff</text>\n  <text x=\"396\" y=\"496\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Bench: wide gap</text>\n  <text x=\"236\" y=\"514\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Draw: V points uphill</text>\n  <text x=\"14\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Spur: V points downhill</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Find each shape here before you go on.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation on a contour map. A deer comes over the ridge at the saddle, the low point between two peaks, walks down the slope and stops on a bench, a flat step with wide spaced lines. It beds there with a view of the slope below. Saddles are crossings, benches are beds.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 150 C 120 144, 280 156, 400 150 L400 205 C 280 212, 120 200, 0 206 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"18\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"18\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 50 C 170 20, 50 12, 50 60 C 50 108, 170 100, 200 74 C 230 100, 350 108, 350 60 C 350 12, 230 20, 200 50 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M0 110 C 100 118, 300 118, 400 110\"/><path d=\"M0 128 C 100 134, 300 134, 400 128\"/><path d=\"M0 150 C 120 144, 280 156, 400 150\"/>\n    <path d=\"M0 206 C 120 200, 280 212, 400 205\"/><path d=\"M0 222 C 120 216, 280 228, 400 221\"/><path d=\"M0 238 C 120 232, 280 244, 400 237\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M0 278 C 120 270, 280 286, 400 276\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">creek</text>\n  <path id=\"hf-saddle-bench-path\" d=\"M200 6 C 200 40, 196 60, 200 80 S 210 130, 180 160 S 140 176, 130 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 6\"/>\n  <g>\n    <ellipse rx=\"14\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M-3 -17 l-4 -7 M3 -17 l4 -7\" stroke=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <animateMotion dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\"><mpath href=\"#hf-saddle-bench-path\"/></animateMotion>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"8\" y=\"4\" width=\"170\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"93\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Crosses at the saddle</text>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"222\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"115\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Beds on the bench (Tip)</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Over the saddle, down to the bench. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Saddles are crossings. Benches are beds (65%, hunter observation).</li><li>Glass benches from across the draw (Tip).</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four slopes drawn at true angle over the same 500 metres of ground. 4 percent is a gentle stroll. 12 percent is a steady climb. 20 percent is hard work. 40 percent is hands on, pick another line.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same 500 m of ground, true angle</text>\n  <g stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\">\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"73\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"169\" stroke=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"215\" y=\"70\" font-weight=\"bold\">4 percent</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"88\">1 line per cm: stroll</text>\n    <text x=\"215\" y=\"124\" font-weight=\"bold\">12 percent</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"142\">3 lines: steady climb</text>\n    <text x=\"215\" y=\"184\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">20 percent</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"202\">5 lines: hard</text>\n    <text x=\"215\" y=\"244\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">40 percent</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"262\">10 lines: hands on</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lines per cm at a 20 m interval</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Count lines per cm before a dawn climb (Tip).</li><li>Follow one contour line to stay flat and quiet (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: steepness table and maths</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lines per cm, 20 m interval</th><th>Rise over 500 m</th><th>Slope</th><th>Walking</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>20 m</td><td>4 percent</td><td>Easy stroll</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>60 m</td><td>12 percent</td><td>Steady climb</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>100 m</td><td>20 percent</td><td>Hard, hands free</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>200 m</td><td>40 percent</td><td>Hands on, pick another line</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Percent slope is rise divided by run <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. 100 m up over 500 m along is 20 percent.</li><li>20 percent feels steep with a pack and a rifle. 40 percent is scrambling (Tip).</li><li>Count lines between the truck and your bench before you commit to a dawn climb (Tip).</li><li>A route that follows one contour line is flat. Side hilling on a contour is the quiet way around a slope (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a hill with north at the top. The north face is dark with timber: shade, cool, bedding. The south and west faces are open and sunny: October feed, warmth and winter range. The sun sits low in the south.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 150 A 140 110 0 0 1 340 150 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 150 A 140 110 0 0 0 340 150 Z\" fill=\"#f2e3b3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <polygon points=\"130,110 140,82 150,110\"/><polygon points=\"170,95 180,66 190,95\"/><polygon points=\"215,92 225,64 235,92\"/><polygon points=\"255,108 265,80 275,108\"/><polygon points=\"195,128 205,100 215,128\"/>\n  </g>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text>\n  <polygon points=\"192,40 208,40 200,28\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">North face</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shade, timber,</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bedding (Tip)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">South face (and west)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sun, feed, winter range</text>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"278\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"258\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"250\"/><line x1=\"178\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"266\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"266\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">low October sun, south</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>South and west faces: October sun and feed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>North faces: shade and bedding timber (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: aspect details</summary><ul><li>Aspect is the compass direction a slope faces <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Find it by picturing water running down across the lines.</li><li>South and west faces catch October sun: feed, warmth, early snow melt <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Interior mule deer <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Winter range\">Winter range</button> sits on south and west aspects in old Douglas fir <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>North faces stay shaded and cool: bedding timber, late snow (Tip).</li><li>The best October benches face south or southwest with timber above them <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Hunter observation.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quick check, side by side. Left: a ridge, contour Vs point downhill, no water. Right: a draw, contour Vs point uphill and a creek runs in it. High ground is at the top of both.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\">\n    <path d=\"M40 60 L102 130 L165 60\"/><path d=\"M30 100 L102 180 L175 100\"/><path d=\"M20 140 L102 230 L185 140\"/>\n    <path d=\"M215 120 L297 60 L380 120\"/><path d=\"M215 170 L297 110 L380 170\"/><path d=\"M215 220 L297 160 L380 220\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M297 56 C 293 120, 302 180, 297 248\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ridge</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Draw</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V points down</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dry spine</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V points up</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">water runs in it</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Read the lines before you read the leaves. The map tells you where to look. Your boots confirm it.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Mixing up ridge and draw. Water runs in draws, never on ridges.</li><li>Trusting green. Cutblocks and burns change it.</li><li>A straight line across ten lines in a centimetre.</li></ul></aside>","<details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><ul><li>Mixing up ridge and draw. The V points uphill for a draw and downhill for a ridge. Water runs in draws, never on ridges.</li><li>Trusting the colour green. Green means trees on the day the map was made. Cutblocks and burns change it.</li><li>Planning a straight line that crosses ten lines in a centimetre.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>On a known ridge, find the saddle, the nearest draw and a bench below you. Say which way the Vs point. Repeat until boring.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://natural-resources.canada.ca/maps-tools-publications/maps/topographic-maps/topographic-maps-tips-hints\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Natural Resources Canada, Topographic maps: tips and hints</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: scale, contour spacing, numbers read uphill, water flow symbols, green and white.</li><li><a href=\"https://natural-resources.canada.ca/maps-tools-publications/maps/topographic-maps/national-topographic-system-maps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Natural Resources Canada, National Topographic System maps</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: 1:50,000 coverage, brown contours.</li><li>Contour interval of 20 m on newer sheets: search preview of the CanTopo 1:50,000 specification <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Deer use of benches, saddles and aspects: Hunt Mentor deer research notes, research/2026-10-01-deer.md, winter range and bedding lines (Armleder 1994, Germaine 2004), plus hunter observation labelled Tip.</li></ul>"]